    "topic": {
      "post_stream": {
        "posts": [
          {
            "id": 597226,
            "name": "",
            "username": "_venacline",
            "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/_/5f9b8f/{size}.png",
            "created_at": "2026-10-08T21:37:42.079Z",
            "cooked": "<p>Hello everyone,</p>\n<p>I’m currently running n8n locally via Docker Desktop to learn the ropes. I want to build my skills on n8n and would love to collaborate on projects to see how others use the platform and understand their thought process behind the problems they solve.</p>\n<p>Right now, I’m not looking for paid gigs yet; instead, I am looking for hands-on, real-world experience. I would love to team up with someone as an assistant or collaborator. You can hand off the repetitive parts of a project to me like mapping out data, setting up credentials or handling webhooks which frees up your time and in return, I get to see how you architecture the final solution.</p>\n<p>While I’m still learning live server hosting, I can confidently handle local testing, setting up API credentials and building workflows to move data around. I am also comfortable working with webhooks and while I haven’t deployed them in production yet, I regularly use ReqBin to send and test POST requests locally. I also have foundational understanding of the Code node(JavaScript) for simple data manipulation.</p>\n<p>Once a workflow is built on my end, I can easily export the JSON file directly to you. I’m looking forward to connecting with experienced developers and working on some great projects together!! Please drop a comment or send me a DM if you’d like to collaborate.</p>\n<p>Thanks,<br>\nVenacline.</p>",
            "post_number": 1,
            "post_type": 1,
            "posts_count": 2,
            "updated_at": "2026-10-08T21:37:42.079Z",
            "reply_count": 0,
